center;verticalAlign=middle;arcSize=3;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="756" width="210" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c1448" value="Free: IO2, IO18, IO42, IO47, IO48. Not used: IO3, IO45, IO46 (strapping), IO35–37 (PSRAM)." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=9;fontColor=#555555;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontStyle=0;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="792" width="460" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c1449" value="Notes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Power&lt;br&gt;• USB-C needs R4/R5 (5.1 kΩ on CC1/CC2) or chargers won&#x27;t give 5 V.&lt;br&gt;• MCP73831 charge current = 1000 / R6 (kΩ) mA. 2.0 kΩ = 500 mA (battery ≥ 500 mAh).&lt;br&gt;• MCP73831 STAT rises to VBUS (5 V) when charging is done: LED only, never to a GPIO.&lt;br&gt;• Q2 DMG2305UX: source → VSYS, drain → VBAT, gate → VBUS with R8 to GND. Wrong way round,&lt;br&gt;  its body diode connects the battery all the time.&lt;br&gt;• Use a LiPo with a built-in protection board. JST-PH polarity is not standard: check it.&lt;br&gt;• AP2112K-3.3: 600 mA, 250 mV dropout. SW3 switches EN only, so charging works while off.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Signals&lt;br&gt;• LCD SPI on the FSPI IO MUX pins (IO10/11/12). ST7789V datasheet: 66 ns write cycle (≈15 MHz);&lt;br&gt;  many panels run at 40 MHz — test.&lt;br&gt;• LIS3DH: CS → 3V3 (I2C), SA0 → GND (0x18), RES → GND. INT1 on IO7 wakes the ESP32 from deep sleep.&lt;br&gt;• ICS-43434: LR → GND (left). 100 kΩ pull-down on SD (datasheet).&lt;br&gt;• microSD (optional): 10 kΩ pull-ups on CMD and DAT0–3, SDMMC 1-bit on IO39/40/41.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hand soldering&lt;br&gt;• LIS3DH and ICS-43434 are LGA: pads under the chip — hot air or a hot plate with solder paste.&lt;br&gt;• ESP32 module EPAD: hot air, or a via hole in the pad to solder it from the back.&lt;br&gt;• USB-C (0.5 mm pins): drag-solder with flux, solder the shell tabs first.&lt;br&gt;• Passives 0805; switches, J2, J3 through-hole.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Layout&lt;br&gt;• Keep copper, the battery and the display&#x27;s metal frame away from the module antenna.&lt;br&gt;• D+/D− as a short 90 Ω pair. Decoupling caps next to their pins (C1/C2 at U1, C12/C13 at U5, C14 at U6).&lt;br&gt;• Keep the I2S and SPI clocks away from the mic and short." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1a1a1a;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontStyle=0;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="80" width="1040" height="600" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>